NUMEROLOGY 
133.3     Divination systems
============================================================
🔢 What numerology is
Numerology is a symbolic interpretive system that assigns
meaning to numbers derived from birth dates and names. It is
not a science; it is a structured symbolic framework blending:

- Pythagorean number philosophy
- Chaldean numerology
- Hebrew gematria
- Modern divination systems

Numbers encode archetypal patterns that map to personality,
motivation, and life trajectory.

🧩 Core idea
Numbers from your birth date and full name are reduced to 
single digits (1–9), except for “master numbers” 11, 22, and 
33. Each digit corresponds to a symbolic theme—leadership, 
intuition, creativity, discipline, etc. 

  Core Objects
  ----------------------------------------------------------
  LIFE PATH        -> birth‑date reduction
  DESTINY          -> full‑name reduction
  SOUL URGE        -> vowel‑reduction
  PERSONALITY      -> consonant‑reduction
  BIRTHDAY         -> day‑of‑month archetype

All numerology reduces numbers to single digits (1–9), except
for master numbers 11, 22, 33.

Digit reduction:
    N → sum_of_digits(N)
    Repeat until N ∈ {1..9, 11, 22, 33}

Birth date → Life Path Number  
Full name → Destiny Number  
Vowels → Soul Urge Number  
Consonants → Personality Number  
Birth day → Birthday Number

Each object corresponds to a distinct interpretive operator:

      operator_LP : person → global trajectory
      operator_DN : person → functional talents
      operator_SU : person → internal drives
      operator_PN : person → external presentation
      operator_BD : person → innate trait‑accent

  DIGIT ARCHETYPES (1–9)
============================================================

  1 : Independence / Initiation / Vector‑Origin
  2 : Harmony / Duality / Relational Coupling
  3 : Creativity / Expression / Expansion
  4 : Structure / Order / Constraint‑Grid
  5 : Freedom / Change / Mobility
  6 : Responsibility / Care / Stabilization
  7 : Analysis / Introspection / Depth‑Probe
  8 : Power / Ambition / Executive Force
  9 : Compassion / Completion / Global Reach

  MASTER NUMBERS (non‑reduced)
============================================================
🕯 Master Numbers (11, 22, 33)
These are not reduced because they’re considered especially 
potent:

  11 : Intuition / Illumination / Signal‑Amplification
  22 : Master Builder / System‑Architect / Macro‑Execution
  33 : Teacher / Compassion‑Vector / Service‑Field

  DIGIT REDUCTION RULE
============================================================
🧮 How calculations work
All numerology uses digit reduction:
Add digits until you reach 1–9.
Keep 11, 22, 33 intact.
Names use letter-to-number mappings (A=1, B=2 … I=9, J=1, etc.).

  Let N be any integer or letter‑sum.

      Reduce:  N → sum_of_digits(N)
      Repeat until N ∈ {1..9, 11, 22, 33}

  Example:
      1984 → 1+9+8+4 = 22  (stop: master number)

  NAME MAPPING (Pythagorean)
============================================================
Letter → Number mapping:
Name‑sum → Destiny Number

  A=1  B=2  C=3  D=4  E=5  F=6  G=7  H=8  I=9
  J=1  K=2  L=3  M=4  N=5  O=6  P=7  Q=8  R=9
  S=1  T=2  U=3  V=4  W=5  X=6  Y=7  Z=8

  Vowels: A, E, I, O, U  (for Soul Urge)
  Consonants: all others (for Personality)

  SYSTEM VIEW (structural)
============================================================
Numerology treats digits as archetypal modes:

      mode_1 .. mode_9, plus master_modes {11,22,33}

Each mode acts like a symbolic operator:

      mode_k : person → thematic tendencies

Birth‑date → global operator (Life Path)  
Name‑sum  → functional operator (Destiny)  
Vowels    → internal‑drive operator (Soul Urge)  
Consonants→ external‑presentation operator (Personality)

Life Path Number
============================================================
Life Path Number = reduced sum of:
    month + day + year

Master numbers (11, 22, 33) remain intact.
